# Coding Standards

## `static volatile`

- Don't reach for `static volatile` by default. If you don't have to use it,
  don't. Prefer plain stack locals when the value never crosses an interrupt
  boundary.
- Use `volatile` only when state is genuinely shared across an ISR boundary
  (or is otherwise modified outside the normal flow of execution, e.g. by
  hardware).
